UID:pretalx-pycon-portugal-2025-HAD3VX@pretalx.evolutio.pt
DTSTART;TZID=WET:20250726T133000
DTEND;TZID=WET:20250726T153000
DESCRIPTION:[Polars](https://github.com/pola-rs/polars) is lightning fast\,
  easy to use\, dataframe library.\nIt's clean API and its contexts and exp
 ressions allow writing readable but performant data wrangling code.\n\nAim
 ed at both data newbies and pandas experts (Polars != pandas)\, in this ha
 nds-on tutorial we'll use data from the [Pokémon franchise](https://en.wi
 kipedia.org/wiki/Pokémon) to explore the Polars API and the ideas that se
 t it apart from pandas and other dataframe libraries.
DTSTAMP:20261116T111145Z
LOCATION:D -112\, Floor -1 (Room Madeira)
SUMMARY:The Pokémon trainer's guide to Polars - Rodrigo Girão Serrão
URL:https://pretalx.evolutio.pt/pycon-portugal-2025/talk/HAD3VX/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pretalx-pycon-portugal-2025-EMWGJK@pretalx.evolutio.pt
DTSTART;TZID=WET:20250726T160000
DTEND;TZID=WET:20250726T180000
DESCRIPTION:Decorators are often thought of as functions that accept functi
 ons as arguments and that return other functions...\n\nIn this hands-on wo
 rkshop you will see that this is not always right.
DTSTAMP:20261116T111145Z
LOCATION:D -114\, Floor -1 (Room Azores)
SUMMARY:Advanced decorators – decorators & classes - Rodrigo Girão Serrão
URL:https://pretalx.evolutio.pt/pycon-portugal-2025/talk/EMWGJK/
END:VEVENT
